{
  "dom_id": "step-q225021",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $\u0394$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\n\u0394={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=v-u,\\,y=u(u+v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{2}$ under the action of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=x(t),\\,y=1+t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nFind the function $x(t).$",
  "worked_solution": "To map the entire region $\u0394$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{2}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{2},$ we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(v-u,\\,u(u+v)) \\\\  & =(v-1,\\,1(1+v)) \\\\  & =(v-1,1+v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{2}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=v-1,\\,y=1+v,\\,0\\le v\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t-1,\\,y(t)=1+t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$",
